# scripts/opcount: `askbench bench strict N` reads a model's strict JSON
# reply N times with llm.Parse (wf10 L6); the cost of one read is the slope
# between the two sizes. The control is hand Go: encoding/json into the
# record's struct. Against ../decode (json.Decode of the same text), the
# bar is 1.10x: Parse's strict path is Decode's one pass.
unit reply
sizes 20000 120000
args bench strict {n}
control benchmarks/llmask/testdata/control
